HI Priya,

Typically using two scales for the y axis is frowned upon. There's lots of discussion online as to why; you could start reading about it with Hadley's comment on Stack Overflow here <https://stackoverflow.com/a/3101876/10360182>. Because of that, it isn't possible to do with ggplot2. If you really need to plot both data in the same chart, instead of splitting them (e.g. with facets), you'll have to use the base plot() function + par() and mess with the margins to get them to line up correctly. Something like:

plot(x,y)
par(new=TRUE, mar=c(1,1,1,1)
plot(y)

